# "If one of the target creatures is an illegal target when Switcheroo resolves, the exchange won't happen" (its ruling;
# CR 701.12a: if the entire exchange can't be completed, no part of it occurs; CR 608.2b). Bot1 casts Switcheroo on its
# Ornithopter and Bot2's Llanowar Elves; in response Bot2 bolts the Ornithopter. Switcheroo resolves with one legal target
# left, and Bot2 keeps the Elves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Island
Ornithopter
Switcheroo
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Forest x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Switcheroo.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Switcheroo; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Ruby; Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
